<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bahrain Island</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Awal</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahrain">Bahrain</a> Island, known in medieval Arabic sources as Awal, is the largest island of the Bahrain archipelago in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persian-gulf">Persian Gulf</a> and the site of the capital, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manama">Manama</a>. Fresh springs and date groves made it a centre of settlement since the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dilmun">Dilmun</a> civilisation. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> its pearl banks were among the richest in the world, and it was ruled in turn by powers based on the nearby Arabian coast of al-Ahsa and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qatif">Qatif</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bahrain-island.jpg" alt="Bahrain Island" width="320" height="749" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Axelspace Corporation · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bahrain_(satellite_view).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
